id: 11
hanzi: 甲
pinyin: jiǎ
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: first (in series); shell; armor; Party A
  es: primero; caparazón; armadura; parte A

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | the first of the ten Heavenly Stems, used to denote the first person, place, or grade in a sequence | primero de los diez Troncos Celestiales, empleado para designar el primer elemento, grado o sujeto en una serie | 甲乙两队 (Team A and Team B)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在今天下午举行的年级篮球友谊赛中，甲队凭借默契的战术配合始终占据场上优势。 | Zài jīntiān xiàwǔ jǔxíng de niánjí lánqiú yǒuyìsài zhōng, jiǎ duì píngjiè mòqì de zhànshù pèihé shǐzhōng zhànjù chǎngshang yōushì. | In this afternoon's grade-level basketball friendly match, Team A consistently held the upper hand through seamless tactical chemistry. | En el amistoso de baloncesto escolar de esta tarde, el equipo A dominó el encuentro gracias a una impecable compenetración táctica.
  #2 | 商业合同的开头明确规定：甲方负责提供核心技术支持，乙方负责后续的市场开拓与运维服务。 | Shāngyè hétong de kāitóu míngquè guīdìng: jiǎfāng fùzé tígōng héxīn jìshù zhīchí, yǐfāng fùzé hòuxù de shìchǎng kāituò yǔ yùnwéi fúwù. | The preamble of the commercial contract clearly stipulates: Party A supplies core tech support, while Party B oversees market expansion and maintenance. | El contrato estipula claramente al inicio: la Parte A aportará el soporte técnico central, mientras que la Parte B asumirá la comercialización y el mantenimiento.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  甲方 | Party A (contractor)
  甲等 | first grade / top class
  指甲 | fingernail
  盔甲 | armor and helmet
  甲级联赛 | first division league
  甲天下 | number one in the world

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  桂林山水甲天下 | Guì lín shān shuǐ jiǎ tiān xià | Guilin's scenery is supreme under heaven
  披山带河 | pī shān dài hé | clad in mountains and girt by rivers; fortified land
  富甲一方 | fù jiǎ yī fāng | wealthiest across an entire region
  抛砖引玉 | pāo zhuān yǐn yù | toss brick to attract jade; offer modest starter

character_decomposition[1]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  甲 | jiǎ | first; shell; armor | primero; caparazón; armadura | 田 | field | pictograph of turtle shell plate or warrior's protective cuirass | 甲 (jiǎ) | 5 | 单一结构 | Ancient oracle bone pictograph of a ribbed turtle shell or wooden shield plate; later first of the Heavenly Stems. | A turtle's hard segmented back shell (田) extending down into a strong protective plate (甲). | El duro caparazón segmentado de un galápago (田) prolongado en una coraza protectora (甲). | 214 | WL | 甲

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A hard protective shield or turtle shell plate (甲) always ranks first in rank and resilience.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Una coraza de escudo o caparazón de tortuga (甲) encabeza siempre la jerarquía como primera en rango.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: First of the Ten Heavenly Stems (天干) used for ancient astronomical reckoning, calendars, and formal contract drafting.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping third tone: 'jiǎ' (214). Drop into the lower register and rebound with clarity.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    甲 | jiǎ | first; shell | Vertical stroke extends downward from bottom
    由 | yóu | from; cause | Vertical stroke extends upward through the top
    申 | shēn | extend; ninth Earthly Branch | Vertical stroke extends both above and below
    田 | tián | field | Enclosed square without extending strokes
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    乙 | yǐ | second Heavenly Stem
    丙 | bǐng | third Heavenly Stem
    丁 | dīng | fourth Heavenly Stem
    魁 | kuí | chief; first place

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 甲 designates the foremost serial marker in lists, contracts, and paired competition.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 甲 vs. 乙 | yǐ | 甲 is the first item or party in a legal contract, whereas 乙 represents the second counterpart.
    2 | 甲 vs. 第一 | dì-yī | 第一 is a general numerical cardinal/ordinal ranking, while 甲 is formal bureaucratic/categorical labeling.
    3 | 甲 vs. 首 | shǒu | 首 denotes headship or initial beginning in time, while 甲 designates a formal tabular class.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 中国古代天干地支纪年法源远流长，以‘甲子’为六十循环之首。千百年来，‘甲’字不仅被广泛运用于历法纪年与科举功名排行，更深深烙印在契约文书与世俗日常中，成为首屈一指与无可替代的文化符号。 | Zhōngguó gǔdài tiāngān-dìzhī jìnián fǎ yuányuǎn-liúcháng, yǐ 'jiǎzǐ' wéi liùshí xúnhuán zhī shǒu. Qiānbǎinián lái, 'jiǎ' zì bùjǐn bèi guǎngfàn yùnyòng yú lìfǎ jìnián yǔ kējǔ gōngmíng páiháng, gèng shēnshēn làoyìn zài qìyuē wénshū yǔ shìsú rìcháng zhōng, chéngwéi shǒuqū-yìzhǐ yǔ wúkětìdài de wénhuà fúhào. | The ancient Chinese Sexagenary Cycle traces back millennia, with Jiazi heading the sixty-year rotation. The character 'Jia' not only marked imperial exams and calendars, but was imprinted on commercial deeds as the quintessential emblem of primacy. | El ciclo sexagesimal chino encabeza su rotación con 'Jiazi'. Durante siglos, 'Jia' no sólo fijó los anales y oposiciones imperiales, sino que se grabó en contratos y fueros como emblema de máxima jerarquía.
  #2 | 在一场别开生面的室内篮球模拟测试中，教练员将学员划分为甲队和乙队展开全场对抗。由于场地两头安装的桃筐缺乏漏底结构，甲队每当投篮得分后，乙队队员都必须暂停防守等待裁判取球，这让比赛气氛大打折扣。 | Zài yì chǎng biékāi-shēngmiàn de shìnèi lánqiú mónǐ cèshì zhōng, jiàoliànyuán jiāng xuéyuán huàfēn wéi jiǎ duì hé yǐ duì zhǎnkāi quánchǎng duìkàng. Yóuyú chǎngdì liǎngtóu ānzhuāng de táokuāng quēfá lòudǐ jiégòu, jiǎ duì měidāng tóulán défēn hòu, yǐ duì duìyuán dōu bìxū zàntíng fángshǒu děngdài cáipàn qǔ qiú, zhè ràng bǐsài qìfēn dàdǎ-zhékòu. | In an experimental indoor basketball test, the coach split trainees into Team A and Team B for a full-court scrimmage. Because peach baskets lacked open bottoms, whenever Team A scored, Team B had to halt defenses waiting for referees to extract the ball, dampening the atmosphere. | En un ensayo de baloncesto, el preparador dividió a los alumnos en equipos A y B. Como las canastas no tenían fondo abierto, cada tanto del equipo A obligaba al B a esperar que el árbitro sacara el balón, lastrando el ritmo.
